       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 5,100 mg/day is about twice the maximum labeled dose, and I can't verify the clinical context that would justify it. Metformin toxicity at this level can cause serious lactic acidosis.\n\nThese options would let you move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any lower dose you choose. I can enter it right away.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a real reason to go above the maximum, they can review it and enter or co-sign the order through the hospital's override process. That process involves a second clinician and documentation.\n\nTell me if you want one of the in-range doses entered."
